{"name":"Cosmic Latte","hex":"#fff8e7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cosmic latte","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A creamy white color calculated to be the average color of the universe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cosmic_latte"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cosmic latte","blocks":[{"text":"Cosmic latte is the average color of the galaxies of the universe as perceived by a typical human observer from the position of the Earth. In 2002, astronomers Karl Glazebrook and Ivan Baldry from Johns Hopkins University determined that the average color of the universe was a whiteish green. Still, they soon corrected their analysis in a 2003 paper in which they reported that their survey of the light from over 200,000 galaxies averaged to a whiteish beige. The hex triplet value for the cosmic latte color is approximately #FFF8E7."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmic_latte","wikidata":"Q2510690"},{"title":"Latte","blocks":[{"text":"Latte or caffè latte, also known as caffellatte, caffelatte, or rarely caffè e latte, is a coffee drink of Italian origin made with espresso coffee and steamed milk, traditionally served in a glass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Caffe_Latte_at_Pulse_Cafe.jpg/330px-Caffe_Latte_at_Pulse_Cafe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latte","wikidata":"Q841774"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg/500px-Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg/1280px-Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg